  "knowledge_gaps": [
    "The baseline terminal-mask frequency and loss reduction are unspecified. A 50% mixture may not increase terminal supervision, and changing position averaging to example averaging introduces a second intervention unless a matched control is retrained.",
    "Uniform random cutoffs change context lengths, target exposure and supervised-target counts. They align endpoint prediction but do not preferentially emphasize recent events; gains cannot automatically be attributed to recency.",
    "Reproduction requires explicit handling of short histories, zero-target random-mask examples, negative tensor construction, provenance synchronization and fresh-process checkpoint–predictor parity.",
    "Checkpoint selection, validation-query frequency and GPU-budget allocation are unspecified. The reported 0.5425 needs confirmation as the pinned macro validation HR@10 before use as a comparator. Sampled HR@10 cannot establish improvements in full-catalog usefulness or compatibility.",
    "Originality 3 is reasonable for established terminal masking. Potential 8 is optimistic without validation evidence; difficulty 3 understates the work needed for controlled comparisons and integrity checks."
  ],
  "follow_up_queries": [
    {
      "reason": "Establish what differs from existing BERT4Rec training and distinguish endpoint alignment from recency weighting.",
      "query": "In BERT4Rec (Sun et al., 2019), how are last-item-only training examples generated and mixed with random masked-item examples? What evidence distinguishes uniform random-prefix terminal masking from explicit recency-weighted sampling in sequential recommendation?"
    },
    {
      "reason": "Resolve loss-weighting and supervision-volume confounds before interpreting the proposed 50% mixture.",
      "query": "For BERT4Rec mixing single-terminal-target examples with multi-target random-mask examples, how do per-token versus per-sequence loss averaging change effective example weights and gradient contributions? What controlled ablations separate masking strategy, context-length distribution and supervised-target count?"
    },
    {
      "reason": "Define defensible conclusions and uncertainty reporting without changing the pinned evaluator or training seed.",
      "query": "What do sampled sequential-recommendation evaluation studies show about HR@10 with 99 negative candidates versus full-catalog ranking, and how should paired user-level uncertainty and repeated validation-based model selection be reported for a fixed four-category macro-average with 200 validation users per category?"
    }
  ]
